PATCH 324: promote + reconstruct the missing 22dd render-script handler 0x3a68 (the RETICLE-GRATICULE
loop) + fix the base-losses in its line/pixel drawers 3d4c / 3a92 / 3d99, so the phase-0x22 render
script advances past it (asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin, DS=SS=DGROUP=0x1c00).

CONTEXT (asm + gdb verified).  The 459a mission loop renders each frame via FUN_0000_22dd, a threaded-code
interpreter `c450=3; do { call word[DGROUP:word[0x4a86]] } while(c450!=0)` that walks a per-phase script
table (cursor DAT_2000_0a86; each handler advances the cursor +2; 23ce terminates).  Patches 322/323 got
the loop iterating (c452 1->314) but it then reaches the phase-0x22 handler 0x3a68 -- a 22dd script
MID-ENTRY Ghidra never promoted (g_mem[0x3a67]==0xc3, not a leading nop), so fist_icall_near(0,0x3a68)
missed the fmap and returned the no-op trap -> the interpreter cursor never advanced past it -> 22dd spun
-> the frame never completed.  EXACT same class as 41df (patch 322) / 41d0 (patch 193) / 378e (patch 194).

0x3a68 (asm 0x3a68-0x3a91, verified):
  word[0x4b9e]=0; loop { es=ds; si=word[0x4b9e]; di=0x6bbe; call near [DGROUP:0x1630];
    if CF -> 3a62 (addw 2,[0x4a86]; ret); word[0x4b9e]=si;
    bx=0x6bc8; call 3d4c;  bx=0x6bc0; call 3a92; }
The iterator near [DGROUP:0x1630]=0xc33c is the SAME object-roster walker FUN_0000_378e uses (patch 292).
As in 378e (patch 292 Block B) the loop MUST store the ITERATOR-RETURNED si (g_fist_iter_si, always
0xffff), not the pre-call si -- otherwise c33c re-INITs every iteration and never signals empty (CF),
flooding op 0x1c.  With the returned si stored, c33c's phase index climbs to exhaustion -> CF=1 -> 3a68
terminates and 22dd returns.  CF via g_fist_cf, returned si via g_fist_iter_si (both existing shim globals).

FUN_0000_3d4c (asm 0x3d4c, the reticle line-endpoint delta builder) -- TWO Ghidra defects, both reached
for the first time now: (1) param_1 (=bx) is a DGROUP NEAR OFFSET (call sites pass 0x6bc8 etc.), typed
`uint *` and dereferenced as a HOST pointer -> rebase g_mem+0x1c000+(uint16)off; (2) `uint *` indexing is
4-byte-scaled (int==4B here) so param_1[1..3] read bx+4/+8/+12, but the asm reads 16-bit words at
bx+0/+2/+4/+6 (X.lo/X.hi/Y.lo/Y.hi) -> read via a uint16_t*.  (3) `DAT_2000_2c38 = uVar1` was wrong (asm
`mov [0x6c38],cx` stores 3d99's half-1 CX result, not the sign flags) -> store the CX 3d99 now publishes.

FUN_0000_3d99 (asm 0x3d99, the two-half line clipper): asm saves half-1's db5 result (`push ax` @0x3dbe)
and restores it into CX (`pop cx` @0x3de0) while AX returns half-2's result.  The __allregs model threaded
only AX -> the CX output was dropped.  Publish half-1's db5 result in the new shim global g_fist_r_cx and
return half-2's, so 3d4c's word[0x6c38] store gets the real clipped-X (3a92's column base).

FUN_0000_3a92 (asm 0x3a92, the graticule single-pixel PLOT) -- base-losses: word[0x156a] is a NEAR OFFSET
P (the dst-geom descriptor), Ghidra's `DAT_1000_d56a` derefs it as a host pointer -> rebase g_mem+0x1c000+P
for the height word[P+0xa], width word[P+0xc] AND the target FRAMEBUFFER SEGMENT word[P] (asm 0x3a9a
`mov es,[di]`, which Ghidra DROPPED on the stos); the scanline rowtable read `word[DGROUP: di*2+word[0x794]]`
was host-dereferenced -> rebase; the pixel store `es:[di]` lost its es(fb-seg) base -> g_mem+(es<<4)+off;
the marker copy `word[0x6b72]=word[bx+2]` host-dereferenced param_3 -> rebase.

